WEBVTT

00:00:03,730 --> 00:00:09,970
PSA test is the prostate specific antigen test. It's not super accurate. If a person was like,

00:00:09,970 --> 00:00:16,370
oh my PSA test was 1.2 and then I went ahead and thought I'd get it. It was a year ago, it was 1.2

00:00:16,370 --> 00:00:21,170
and now it's 3.4. That does not mean you have prostate cancer. It could be that you have inflammation

00:00:21,170 --> 00:00:29,730
of the prostate. But if you have PSA test of 1.2 a year ago and now it's 140, you know, I have a patient

00:00:29,730 --> 00:00:38,290
coming in Monday, his PSA is 1200. It's not fully, but it's not perfect. So you don't use the PSA test

00:00:38,290 --> 00:00:44,370
to diagnose cancer. But if somebody's PSA changes dramatically in a relatively short period of

00:00:44,370 --> 00:00:48,930
time, that's an indication there's something going on. That's completely an art form. And

00:00:49,570 --> 00:00:56,370
a digital test is, if the doctor is an expert at doing that, you're not going to, you just take

00:00:56,370 --> 00:01:01,170
a chance. Remember, cancer can be the size of a pit head and it's a million cells. So you're not

00:01:01,170 --> 00:01:07,570
going to feel that in a digital test. So there's better ways to test for that.

